From: DoomGuy41 <DoomGuy41@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:16:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Time and alarms without /dev/alarm (timerfd,
 settimeofday, CAP_WAKE_ALARM)

Framework part: AlarmManagerService uses timerfd (CLOCK_*_ALARM), SystemClock.setCurrentTimeMillis
uses settimeofday. The PM8998 RTC refuses writes, so the offset between wall time and the RTC
is saved and re-applied at boot by init.taimen.rc (rtc-restore).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../com/android/internal/os/ZygoteInit.java   |   3 +-
 core/jni/android_os_SystemClock.cpp           |  28 +++-
 ...com_android_server_AlarmManagerService.cpp | 136 +++++++++++++++---
 3 files changed, 144 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

